          "ruleId": "CWE-79",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Stored/reflected DOM XSS via unescaped JSON object KEYS in `json2html`. Attacker-controlled JSON reaches `$.fn.jsonViewer(json, options)` (line 109) -> `json2html(json, options)` (line 122) -> inside json2html the dict branch iterates `_iterator_0 = <operator>.iterator(json)` (line 77) binding `key = _result_0.value`, then builds `var keyRepr = options.withQuotes ? '<span class=\"json-string\">\"' + key + '\"</span>' : key` (lines 80-81) and appends it raw: `html += '<a href class=\"json-toggle\">' + keyRepr + '</a>'` (line 84) and `html += keyRepr` (line 86). The HTML-escaping replace chain (`.replace(/&/g,'&amp;').replace(/</g,'&lt;')...`, line 33) is applied ONLY inside the `typeof json === 'string'` value branch \u2014 `key` never passes through it, and no other escaping call exists in the file. The resulting string is returned to line 122 and written to the DOM with the raw-HTML sink `$(this).html(html)` at line 128 (FLOWS_TO edge arg_index=1 from the line-122 json2html call to the line-128 html call confirms the chain). A JSON payload such as {\"<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>\": 1} executes script in the page.\n\nVerifier (CONFIRM): Re-derived from source: in json2html the HTML-escaping replace chain exists ONLY inside the `typeof json === 'string'` value branch (lines 31-46, replaces at 34-38 and 44). The dict branch (73-99) iterates `for (var key in json)` (77) and builds `keyRepr` from the raw `key` (80-81), emitting it unescaped at line 84 (`'<a href class=\"json-toggle\">' + keyRepr + '</a>'`) and line 86 (`html += keyRepr`). A whole-file grep for replace/escape/DOMPurify/textContent/.text( returns only lines 34-38 and 44, so no sanitizer touches keys. The returned string flows unconditionally from `var html = json2html(json, options)` (122) into the raw-HTML sink `$(this).html(html)` (128) inside the public `$.fn.jsonViewer` API (109); a scoped Cypher query confirms a FLOWS_TO{arg_index:1} edge 122 -> 128. The line-122/128 calls carry reachable_from_entry=false, but that is the documented arrow/anonymous-function under-linking: `json2html` itself is reachable_from_entry=true and an EntryPoint ENTERS_AT target (line 29, exposure \"reachable\"), and the source path is straight-line with no guard, so reach is confirmed by reading the code. A live consumer pattern is in-repo: demo.html:34-45 turns user-pasted text into an object and calls .jsonViewer(input, options). Payload {\"<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>\": 1} takes the line-86 path (isCollapsable(1) is false), emitting the key verbatim into .html() so onerror executes; withQuotes:true is equally vulnerable since key is interpolated raw at line 81. The library escapes values and its CHANGELOG claims \"Escape XML/HTML tags in JSON content\" (:24) and \"Fixed XSS injection\" (:9), so the unescaped key is a real security gap, not accepted design. Version is pinned at 1.4.0 (package.json:3, released 2019-08-19) i.e. not a patched build; exploit_search was unavailable in this environment (\"exploit corpus unavailable: not indexed\"), so no exploit-reference claim is made in either direction and the verdict rests on source+graph evidence alone. The analyst's claimed location is accurate."
          },
